Carrying Capabilities you may have a point, but there is nothing more
fascinating than watching cats attack and defend themselves. They absolutely
fight as if it was a game. I've watched cats attack snakes. As they taunt
the snake, the snake would strike and the cat would jump straight up in the
air and come down and smack the snake in the head with its paws "(claws)".
Over and over till the snake tires of it and tries to leave, but the cat
will not let the snake leave until IT is ready to quit. Smaller things like
squirrels better run for their lives. And most dogs get enough of an attack
cat after its first or second claw in the nose. I know they are not deadly
like dogs, but they are swift and spunky.

If they could grow in size like Nethack allows them too, I would fear them
as much as a dog perhaps.

